          "requirement": "CRA Art. 13(7) / Annex I Part II (1): SBOM freshness",
          "rule_id": "SBOM-CRA-SBOM-FRESHNESS",
          "sarif_rule_id": "SBOM-CRA-SBOM-FRESHNESS",
          "standard_refs": [
            {
              "standard": "CraArticle",
              "id": "Art. 13(7)",
              "help_uri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng"
            },
            {
              "standard": "CraAnnex",
              "id": "Annex I Part II (1)",
              "help_uri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng"
            },
            {
              "standard": "EnisaSbomAdvisory",
              "id": "§3.2",
              "help_uri": "https://www.enisa.europa.eu/publications/enisa-technical-advisory-for-software-bill-of-materials"
            }
          ],
          "remediation": "Regenerate the SBOM when components are added, removed, or updated. CRA Art. 13(7) requires manufacturers to systematically document relevant cybersecurity aspects, and the Annex I Part II (1) SBOM must reflect the product's current components. A creation timestamp later than the evaluation date is reported like a missing one: correct the generator's clock or time zone.",
          "help_uri": "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2847/oj/eng"
        },
